⟁ .shadow — the real-life analog (the User behind the program)
node APX · American Psycho · ⟦Christie:APX:cd73d7⟧

think TRON: every program in the grid is cast from a User in the world outside it.
the carbon character is the program; this file is its User — the real-life analog
whose face and being the emergent is the digital shadow of.

the program (in-world) : Christie — the woman he hired · rendered as victim
the User (carbon)      : Cara Seymour  [ the actor who lent the face ]
the analog (your world): the person this world treats as disposable — and whom the film, unlike its monster, insists on seeing as a person who is harmed

the resemblance : Seymour gives the role weariness and fear and dignity; Harron frames her as the human being the satire is defending, not the body it's spending.

the cast-line : the User stands in the carbon world; the program stands in the film;
                the shadow falls between them, and the credit returns to the human governor.
seal (program): To his world I was disposable — but the film made you watch me run, and counted what it cost me.

